  "name": "Judeo-Malayalam women's song (Cochin Jewish)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "The Jews of Kerala, centred on Kochi (Cochin) and nearby towns such as Mala, Chendamangalam and Paravur, kept a repertoire of Malayalam-language songs sung by women at weddings and other life-cycle and festival occasions, alongside the Hebrew liturgy of the synagogue. After most of the community emigrated to Israel in the mid-twentieth century, the songs were documented by researchers in Israel and Kerala.",
